  .sc-faq-a{ padding:0 22px 20px; font-family:var(--font-text); font-size:14px; color:var(--ink-2); line-height:1.65; max-width:720px; }
</style>
<div style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--bg);">
  <div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding:11px 32px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-3);display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
    <a href="/capabilities" class="hana-link" style="font-size:12.5px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-weight:500;">Capabilities</a>
    <span style="color:var(--line);">&rsaquo;</span>
    <a href="/capabilities/osat" class="hana-link" style="font-size:12.5px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-weight:500;">OSAT</a>
    <span style="color:var(--line);">&rsaquo;</span>
    <span style="color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;">Ultra-small Packages</span>
  </div>
</div>
<details class="cap-mobnav"><summary><span>OSAT Services</span><span class="cap-mobnav-meta">11<span class="cap-mobnav-chev"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></span></summary><div class="cap-mobnav-list"><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Design</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/package-design" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Package Design &amp; Simulation</a><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Packaging solutions</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/power-packages" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Power Packages — SiC &amp; GaN</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/qfn-dfn-lga" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>QFN, DFN &amp; LGA</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/optical-packaging" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Clear &amp; Optical Packaging</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/hermetic-ceramic" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Hermetic &amp; Ceramic Packaging</a><a aria-current="page" href="/capabilities/osat/ultra-small-packages" class="cap-sub-leaf cap-active"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Ultra-small Packages</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/system-in-package" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>System in Package (SiP)</a><div class="cap-sb-glabel">Wafer, assembly &amp; test</div><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-processing" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Processing</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-level-packaging" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Level Packaging</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/flip-chip" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Flip Chip &amp; Interconnect</a><a href="/capabilities/osat/wafer-probe-final-test" class="cap-sub-leaf"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Wafer Probe &amp; Final Test</a><span class="cap-sub-leaf cap-removed"><span class="cap-sub-arr">&#8250;</span>Die Attach &amp; Wire Bond</span></div></details>
<div class="sc-hero-band" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:#fff;position:relative;z-index:1;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band cap-section--hero"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;">
    <div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:14px;">OSAT · Ultra-small Packages</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:46px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-0.03em;margin:0 0 18px;max-width:740px;text-wrap:balance;">Ultra-small Packages</h1>
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:18px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 32px;text-wrap:pretty;">For compact electronics, package dimensions can be a key constraint on the final device. Hana's qualified range extends to sub-millimeter body sizes, with custom package design available where a standard footprint does not meet the application requirements.</p>
    <div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface);width:100%;height:407px;"><img src="/images/photos/cap-osat-ultra-small-packages-hero.webp" alt="Ultra-small sensor and optical packages beside a fingertip for scale" style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center;" /></div>
    <div class="hana-spec-block" style="margin-top:18px;"><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Smallest body in the range</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">0.6 × 1.0 mm</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Thinnest leadless package</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">0.37 mm</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Minimum die size</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">10 × 10 mils</div></div><div class="hana-spec-item"><div class="hana-spec-label" style="display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Placement accuracy</div><div class="hana-spec-value" style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:17px;">±10 µm</div></div></div>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="sc-pillars-band" data-hana-bg="wafer" data-variant="light" data-accent="" data-fade="none" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f5f7fa 35%,#d8e6f3 100%);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Capability overview</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Three parameters define the practical limit: body size, package thickness, and the placement and bonding tolerances needed to build reliably at that scale.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-3"><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="minimize-2" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">How small the body goes</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">The smallest qualified leaded package formats.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">SOD723 at 0.6 × 1.0 mm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">SOT9X3 at 0.8 × 1.0 mm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">SOT5X3 at 1.2 × 1.6 mm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">SC70 at 1.25 × 2.0 mm</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="layers" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">How thin it goes</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">A range of thin-body options, matched to the package architecture.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Standard leadless thicknesses from 0.37 mm to 0.90 mm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Wafer backgrind to 4 mils for the thinnest molded builds</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Film-assist molding to control warpage in thin bodies</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">0.30 mm optical LGA at the thinnest end of the range</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="target" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Placement &amp; bonding tolerances</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">At these dimensions, placement, bonding, and finishing tolerances become increasingly important.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">XY placement accuracy to ±10 µm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Minimum die size of 10 × 10 mil</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Bond-pad pitch down to 45 µm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Chemical de-burr capability to 50 µm</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section" id="package-reference">
<div style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--hana-blue);margin-bottom:12px;">Package reference · live</div>
<h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:32px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.14;letter-spacing:-0.025em;margin:0 0 12px;max-width:740px;">The bodies we list</h2>
<p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:16px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 22px;text-wrap:pretty;">Every leaded body in the portfolio and the automotive-qualified packages that go with them, from 0.6 &times; 1.0 mm upward. Filter by size or grade, or paste what you&rsquo;re building.</p>
<div data-pkgfinder data-embed data-own="/capabilities/osat/ultra-small-packages"></div>
<p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-3);margin:18px 0 0;max-width:660px;">Sizes describe what a package is — family, body size, lead count, automotive grade. <a href="/capabilities/osat/package-finder" style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:600;">Search the whole package reference &rarr;</a></p>
<div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 8px;">The small end of the range</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 20px;">Every size we build can be searched above. Listed here are the leaded bodies at and below 1.2 mm — all already tooled for production.</p><style>.osat-tbl{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--font-text);margin:0}.osat-tbl caption{text-align:left;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);padding:0 0 10px}.osat-tbl th{text-align:left;font-size:10px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);padding:0 16px 8px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.osat-tbl td{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);padding:9px 16px 9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.osat-tbl td:first-child{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500}</style><table class="osat-tbl"><caption>Leaded bodies at and below 1.2 mm</caption><thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Body size</th><th>Lead counts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SOD723</td><td>0.6 × 1.0 mm</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>SOT9X3</td><td>0.8 × 1.0 mm</td><td>3, 5, 6</td></tr><tr><td>SOT5X3</td><td>1.2 × 1.6 mm</td><td>4, 5, 6</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:44px;"><div class="why-grid"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#155F9B 0%,#0E4A7C 46%,#0A3860 100%);border:none;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark-white.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.24);"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">A qualified portfolio that extends below 1.2 mm</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.84);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Hana's qualified portfolio extends below 1.2 mm across both leaded and leadless families, with standard footprints already tooled for production.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Already-tooled standard parts in leaded and leadless families</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Qualified formats extending below 1.2 mm</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">No new package tooling for listed standard footprints</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Custom package design when no standard footprint fits</span></li></ul></div><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#FFFFFF 0%,#E5EEF5 58%,#D8E6F1 100%);border:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:#BFD4E4;"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Ultra-small packages with automotive qualification</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Several of Hana’s smaller leadless package families are automotive-qualified, while SOT23 3L supports Grade 0 operation to the 150 °C class.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">SOT23 3L qualified to Grade 0</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Grade 1 across SC70, SOT553, uDFN, uTDFN, sTDFN, and TDFN</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Qualified copper-wire assembly on MSOP and SOIC</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #CBDCEA;border-bottom:1px solid #CBDCEA;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;">Wettable-flank options for inspectable automotive joints</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Where we run it</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Molded package assembly and test are available across our OSAT network; production mix varies by site.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-4"><a href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">Thailand</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Ayutthaya</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Ayutthaya <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">China</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Jiaxing</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Jiaxing <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;"><details class="sc-faq" open><summary>What is the smallest package you build?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">0.6 × 1.0 mm — available both as a leaded SOD723 and as a leadless DFN.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>How thin can the package be?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Leadless packages start at 0.37 mm nominal. The thinnest in production is a 0.30 mm optical LGA, which is a clear-molded part rather than a standard body.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Can ultra-small parts be automotive-qualified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. SC70, SOT553, uDFN, uTDFN, sTDFN and TDFN are automotive-qualified, and SOT23 3L runs at Grade 0.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What is the smallest die you can handle?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">10 × 10 mils, placed to ±10 µm, with bond pad pitch down to 45 µm. Below that the constraint is usually the pad pitch rather than the die.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What if our design doesn't match a standard footprint?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Hana can develop a custom package, including the leadframe, package outline, and footprint, with thermal and warpage simulation before tooling is cut. If a standard footprint already fits, we build to it.</div></details></div></div></div></div>
